# EAS reads this file from the root of the git repository, not from the app
# (apps/mobile), and archives the whole repository; the build then runs in
# apps/mobile. So paths here are relative to the repository root.
#
# A .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the EAS build archive, it does not add to
# it. So this file has to repeat every .gitignore rule that matters for a build:
# without them the locally prebuilt /ios and /android folders ride along, which
# both bloats the upload (hundreds of MB) and makes EAS classify the project as
# bare workflow, where the "appVersion" runtimeVersion policy is rejected.
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore.

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders (EAS runs prebuild itself)
/apps/mobile/ios
/apps/mobile/android
/.idea

# local app data / backups
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
# bundled read-only reference DB (built by apps/mobile/scripts/build-cities-db.mjs)
!/apps/mobile/assets/db/cities.db
*.mmbak
skills-lock.json
/.agents

# training data
/training
/apps/mobile/training

# Keep the Cloudflare resources (Workers, D1 schemas) out of the EAS build
# context entirely — they are separate server-side deploys (see "Cloudflare" in
# README.md) and are never part of the iOS/Android app bundle.
/apps/cloudflare/

# The local model evals (apps/evals): OpenRouter + Opus judge tooling with a
# rendered dataset, never part of the app.
/apps/evals/

# Repository-level material no build reads: CI workflows and the PR screenshots
# and evidence under .github/pr-assets (100+ MB), and the agent config.
/.github/
/.claude/
/.codex/
